# Ecommerce core standards

Follow these without being asked again.

## Dynamic everything
- Prefer **admin/CMS/site-settings driven** values over hardcoding.
- Brand name, logo, tagline, support phone/email, currencies, languages, countries, shipping, SEO, nav, announcement — read from `SiteSettings` / `getSiteSettings()` / branding helpers.
- Do not hardcode store name as "YourStore", fake phones, or fixed currency lists when settings exist.

## Safe changes
- **Do not run `npm run build`** unless the user explicitly asks. Prefer targeted typecheck/lint or fix-only.
- **Do not break** existing APIs, cart, wishlist, compare, search, filters, sorting, pagination, auth, or admin flows unless the task requires it.
- When the user says UI-only: change UI/UX only — no backend/API contract changes.
- Match existing patterns in the repo before inventing new ones.

## Next.js in this repo
- This Next.js version differs from training data. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and `AGENTS.md` before using unfamiliar APIs.

## Quality bar
- Production-minded, mobile-first, polished UI — not generic template look.
- Long/async work (imports, bulk jobs): show **progress** (done / left / total); prefer **chunked** processing for reliability.
- Filters and lists: normalize messy data (case, aliases, duplicates); show real counts, not zeros from missing fields.
